# Verify GOV.UK Frontend upgrades with tests

When `govuk-frontend` (or closely related Design System assets) is updated, do not finish until regression checks have run.

1. Prefer macros for any HTML/CSS/JS fallout — see `.cursor/rules/govuk-frontend-ui.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/govuk-frontend-theming-overrides.mdc` / `.cursor/rules/govuk-frontend-js-overrides.mdc`
2. Rebuild frontend assets: `yarn build` (or rely on webpack-dev-middleware in `yarn start:dev` for local smoke)
3. Run **unit / integration** suites that cover touched UI and content builders: `yarn test` and relevant focused Jest paths
4. Run **accessibility** where practical: `yarn tests:a11y` (or note if env blocks it)
5. Prefer fuller coverage when the upgrade is large: functional (`yarn test:functional` / tagged groups) and Playwright security under `playwright/tests/` when env allows
6. Manually spot-check critical journeys in the browser if automated suites miss a known layout surface (home, claim issue, response, dashboard)
7. Sync version notes in README / docs in the same change when they mention GOV.UK Frontend

Do not treat Dependabot/Renovate GOV.UK bumps as complete until automated checks pass (or failures are explained with a documented exception).
